# fix symmetry example: SiC with zinc blende structure, Tersoff potential,
# and a two-fold rotation axis along z (space group P2)
#
# Zinc blende is the diamond structure with the two FCC sublattices
# occupied by different elements.  It has no inversion symmetry, since
# inversion would exchange Si and C.  The two-fold rotation about the z
# axis through a Si atom maps each sublattice onto itself.  The Si atoms
# on the axis can only move along z.

units           metal
atom_style      atomic

# basis atoms 1-4 are on one FCC sublattice (Si), 5-8 on the other (C)
lattice         diamond 4.3596
region          box block 0 2 0 2 0 2
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box basis 5 2 basis 6 2 basis 7 2 basis 8 2
mass            1 28.0855
mass            2 12.011

pair_style      tersoff
pair_coeff      * * SiC.tersoff Si C

fix             1 all nve
fix             sym all symmetry p2.json

velocity        all create 600.0 87287 loop geom
run             0 post no
velocity        all scale 600.0

# symmetry indicator for the two-fold axis along z
variable        odd atom sin(2*PI*(x-xlo)/lx)+sin(2*PI*(y-ylo)/ly)
compute         odd all reduce sum v_odd

timestep        0.0005
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal press c_odd
thermo          100
run             1000
